# ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# TASK 36 B2 — THE UPLOAD DIRECTORY DOES NOT RUN CODE.
#
# This directory is the target of the public/storage symlink, so everything
# in it is reachable over HTTP, and everything in it arrived as an upload.
#
# MEASURED, BEFORE THIS FILE EXISTED. Three files were written into
# storage/app/public/media and fetched through the symlink:
#
#   _t36probe.php       -> 200, body "EXECUTED-8.1.17"
#   _t36probe.gif.php   -> 200, body "GIF89aEXECUTED-DISGUISED"
#   _t36probe.phtml     -> 200, served as text (no handler)
#
# The first two RAN. Apache maps any .php in a published directory to the PHP
# handler whatever the rest of the name says, so a file called holiday.gif.php
# is a script, and a GIF header in front of it changes nothing.
#
# Nothing in the application lets such a file be written — MediaUploader
# validates the mime type, re-encodes every image and names the result itself
# from a UUID, so the uploaded filename never reaches the disk (see
# tests/Feature/Security/UploadHardeningTest.php, which proves it by trying).
# This file is the second lock: it means that if that validation is ever
# wrong, the worst case is a downloaded file rather than executed code.
#
# BOTH MECHANISMS, BECAUSE NEITHER IS PORTABLE ALONE. php_flag only exists
# under mod_php and is a fatal error under php-fpm, hence the <IfModule>
# guards; the Require denial works everywhere .htaccess is read at all, and
# is the one that matters.
#
# A SERVER THAT IGNORES .htaccess IGNORES THIS. Under nginx the equivalent is
# a location block for the storage path with no fastcgi_pass. See
# docs/operations/deployment.md.
# ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# Anything that could be a script is not downloadable, let alone runnable.
<FilesMatch "(?i)\.(php|phtml|php[0-9]|phps|pht|phar|cgi|pl|py|rb|sh|bash|exe|jsp|asp|aspx|htaccess|htpasswd)$">
    <IfModule mod_authz_core.c>
        Require all denied
    </IfModule>
    <IfModule !mod_authz_core.c>
        Order allow,deny
        Deny from all
    </IfModule>
</FilesMatch>

# And no interpreter is attached to anything here in the first place.
<IfModule mod_php.c>
    php_flag engine off
</IfModule>
<IfModule mod_php7.c>
    php_flag engine off
</IfModule>
<IfModule mod_php8.c>
    php_flag engine off
</IfModule>

RemoveHandler .php .phtml .php3 .php4 .php5 .php7 .php8 .phps .pht .phar
RemoveType .php .phtml .php3 .php4 .php5 .php7 .php8 .phps .pht .phar

# No directory listings, and no CGI.
Options -ExecCGI -Indexes
